                "This constrained non-linear optimization problem is solved using Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) first-order necessary conditions. The Lagrangian is formulated as: L(x, lambda, mu, nu) = sum_{m=1}^M R_m(x_m) - lambda * (sum x_m - B_total) - sum mu_m * (L_m - x_m) - sum nu_m * (x_m - U_m), where lambda represents the Lagrange multiplier associated with the overall budget constraint (the shadow price of an additional marketing dollar), and mu_m, nu_m represent the KKT multipliers associated with inequality bounds. The KKT stationarity condition mandates that at the optimal budget allocation x^*: (d R_m(x_m^*) / d x_m) - lambda + mu_m - nu_m = 0. Enterprise optimization engines solve this system using Sequential Least Squares Programming (SLSQP) or Interior Point Methods, generating mathematically guaranteed optimal spend allocations in seconds.",
